## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Tern project following the latest official documentation from vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- Package added to dependencies in package.json
- package-lock.json updated with new dependencies

**2. Code Changes**
Modified `app/[locale]/layout.tsx`:
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component before closing `</body>` tag
- Component placed after the NextIntlClientProvider to ensure analytics track all page views

### Implementation Details

The project uses Next.js App Router with internationalization (next-intl), so the Analytics component was added to the root layout file at `app/[locale]/layout.tsx`. This ensures:
- Analytics are tracked across all locales (en, ko, ja, zh)
- The component loads on every page of the application
- Analytics data is collected site-wide

The `<Analytics />` component was placed at the end of the body, following Vercel's best practices for the App Router architecture.

### Next Steps

To activate analytics tracking:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics sidebar → Enable)
3. After deployment, verify tracking by checking the browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`

### Notes

- No environment variables are required for basic setup
- Analytics will automatically track page views once deployed to Vercel
- The build process showed a pre-existing Firebase API key error unrelated to this change
- Linter passed with no errors introduced by these changes
